  "success_stories": "Lemoore Police Department officers responded to a reported domestic violence incident after a victim reported being assaulted by the father of her children. By the time officers began their investigation, the suspect had left the area and his whereabouts were unknown.\nAfter officers determined that a felony domestic violence offense had occurred, an alert was issued on the suspect's vehicle into Flock Safety system. A few hours later, the system alerted dispatch that the vehicle had been detected by a Flock Safety camera within the city.\nUsing the alert information, officers quickly located the vehicle, conducted a traffic stop, and safely took the suspect into custody without incident. The suspect was booked into the Kings County Jail on felony domestic violence charges.\n\nHow Flock Helped:\nFlock Safety provided a timely vehicle alert that helped officers locate a suspect whose whereabouts were unknown, allowing the investigation to be resolved safely and efficiently.\nData & Usage Summary",
